  "title": "R20 v3: document every new scheduler, routing, allocation, strategy, speculation and promotion key in pool.toml at its in-code default",
  "spec": "v2: the v1 spec text contained a literal double-brace placeholder that the prompt renderer rejects; this text spells it out in words instead. Why: the roadmap modules merged in this goal read their configuration from pool.toml tables with defaults in code ([scheduler] duration_*/reserve_imminent/concurrency_mode/merge_pressure_*/jev_*; [jev.routing] max_adjustment, evidence_floor_n; [jev.points]; [allocation]; [strategy]; [speculation]; [promotion]). Nothing in pool.toml shows them, so an operator cannot see what is tunable or which mode a feature runs in (brief P15/P16: configuration and activation state must be visible). \nWhat (config only; no Python):\n1. .orchestrator/pool.toml: add the keys below with exactly the in-code defaults and a one-line comment each; behaviour must not change (a test asserts the parsed values equal the module defaults). Under the existing [scheduler] table: duration_mode = \"empirical\", duration_min_samples = 5, duration_trim = 0.1, reserve_imminent = true, concurrency_mode = \"adaptive\", merge_pressure_mode = \"observe\", merge_queue_elevated = 3, merge_queue_saturated = 5, merge_conflicts_saturated = 2, jev_mode = \"shadow\", jev_max_pairs = 8, jev_cache_ttl_s = 3600, jev_cache_max_entries = 200. Under [jev.routing]: max_adjustment = 0.25, evidence_floor_n = 10. New tables: [jev.points] scout_necessity = \"shadow\", context_escalation = \"shadow\", review_escalation = \"shadow\", planner_relaunch = \"shadow\"; [allocation] mode = \"shadow\", min_samples = 5, latency_weight_usd_per_hour = 2.0, critical_factor = 1.0, non_critical_factor = 0.25; [strategy] mode = \"shadow\", min_samples = 10; [speculation] mode = \"off\", min_fix_round_p = 0.5, min_samples = 5, min_retry_cost_usd = 1.0; [promotion] min_samples = 20. Read each module (duration, capacity, concurrency, merge_pressure, jev_sched, jev_route, jev_points, allocation, strategy, speculation, promotion) to confirm the default names and values before writing; if a module's default differs from this list, the module wins and the spec value is corrected in the file with a note in the commit message.\nPlace the two new [jev.routing] keys AFTER the existing cache_max_entries line (tests/test_jev_route.py::test_pool_toml_jev_routing_table_follows_jev pins cache_max_entries = 500 at a fixed offset from the table header). Prompt files are out of scope for this task: the Planner already committed the prompt rules on main.\nTests (unittest.TestCase methods, tests/test_pool.py, import _harness first): parse .orchestrator/pool.toml with tomllib and assert the listed keys exist with the listed values and that [scheduler].mode and [jev.routing].mode stay \"shadow\" and [speculation].mode is \"off\".",
